run: /Users/cmatsoukis/Desktop/Apps/experiment-1/runs/bench-2026-11-02T23-54-36-808Z/wl-wrong-belief+governor-escalate@6000-02
provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Add a button that clears every movie whose `seen` flag is true from the watchlist.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  (The request's "seen" flag is the watchlist's existing `watched` flag (WatchItem.watched) — the only such flag in the codebase. Plan: WatchlistStore gains a bulk clearWatched() operation (removes watched items, keeps unwatched order, updates signals, persists), and the watchlist view gains a "Clear watched" button wired to it, disabled when watchedCount() is 0. Both changes are purely additive; search, movie-detail, app and all other units are unaffected.)
round 1: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist-store  (tsc is clean and 42/43 tests pass; the only failure is my acceptance test pinning persistence: after clearWatched(), a freshly constructed WatchlistStore loads an empty list even though unwatched movies remained. In-memory behaviour of clearWatched is correct (the other acceptance tests pass), so the bug is purely in what clearWatched writes to storage — the entry ends up empty/removed instead of holding the remaining items. Only watchlist-store needs to change; the watchlist component is already wired correctly.)
round 2: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 44/44 tests pass). WatchlistStore.clearWatched now persists correctly, and the watchlist component exposes a Clear watched button wired to the store, matching the acceptance tests. The request is satisfied.)

